umask
umask [-p] [-S] [mode]
#set the shell process's file creation mask to mode. If mode begins with a digit, it is interpreted as an octal
#number; if not, it is interpreted as a symbolic mode mask similar to that accepted by the chmod command. If mode 
#is ommitted, umask prints the current value of the mask. If the -S option is supplied without a mode argumetn, umask
#prints the mask in a symbolic format; the default output is an octal number. If the -p option is supplied, and mode
#is ommitted, the output is in a form that may be reused as input. the return status is zero if the mode is 
#successfully changed or if no mdoe argument is supplied, and non-zero otherwise.
#When the mdoe is interpreted as an octal number, each number of the umask is subtracted from 7. Thus, a umask of 022 results in permissions 755.

